{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\NextDiary\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-duplicate",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/nextdiary/entry/{id}: nextdiary.page.indexentrypage at appinfo/routes.php:15 routes, nextdiary.page.get_entrylegacy at appinfo/routes.php:62 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 verb and path or route name is declared more than once. The server keeps one route per name and takes the first that matches a request, so the other one is never reached.",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/nextdiary/entry/{id}: nextdiary.page.indexentrypage at appinfo/routes.php:15 routes, nextdiary.page.get_entrylegacy at appinfo/routes.php:62 routes"
      ]
    },
